  "question": {
    "text": "Two poles of height <math><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;meters and <math><mi>b</mi></math> meters stand at the centres of two circular plots which touch each other externally at a point and the two poles subtend angles of <math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mn>30</mn></mrow> <mtext>o</mtext> </msup> </mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mn>60</mn></mrow> <mtext>o</mtext> </msup> </mrow> </math> respectively at this point, then the distance (in meters) between the centres of these plots is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
